00:28:43.410 --> 00:28:46.830
Today, an older boy punched me very hard

00:28:46.830 --> 00:28:48.030
and then gave me a wedgie.

00:28:48.430 --> 00:28:51.010
Then I saw a bug and started to cry.

00:28:51.650 --> 00:28:54.450
I miss you and Daddy and my kitty cat.

00:28:55.340 --> 00:28:56.500
Love Always, Conan.

00:28:56.500 --> 00:29:00.000
October 8, 1993.

00:29:00.830 --> 00:29:18.600
We'll be back with more after this.

00:29:18.680 --> 00:29:19.220
Stick around.

00:29:43.180 --> 00:29:54.570
And I got to say this, Andy, I think you'd agree that we both got to go to some pretty fun places and do some really neat things, all on NBC's dime, which is great.

00:29:54.690 --> 00:29:59.450
Yeah, and I'm glad you mentioned that because I actually made a little highlight reel.

00:30:00.920 --> 00:30:02.620
Oh, wait, well, so did I, actually.

00:30:02.880 --> 00:30:04.960
I made one, too, yeah.

00:30:05.750 --> 00:30:07.280
Okay.

00:30:08.040 --> 00:30:10.980
Well, no, no, I mean, again, again, this is really awkward.

00:30:11.280 --> 00:30:12.440
You know what the thing to do is?

00:30:12.680 --> 00:30:13.520
No, let's be fair.

00:30:13.600 --> 00:30:14.880
Tonight of all nights, let's be fair.

00:30:15.200 --> 00:30:16.080
We'll flip a coin.

00:30:16.180 --> 00:30:16.560
I think I got one.

00:30:16.560 --> 00:30:17.580
Liz, roll my reel!

00:30:19.620 --> 00:30:25.210
Okay, now it's time to let you in on my system.

00:30:26.850 --> 00:30:29.500
I am going to bet on every dog.

00:30:30.670 --> 00:30:37.200
That's right. Every dog to win, across the board. That way, I can't lose.

00:30:37.200 --> 00:30:38.090
Do the math!

00:30:38.090 --> 00:30:55.200
I need your help. It's been good to you.

00:31:00.090 --> 00:31:03.520
I tell you, the best thing about coming to Hawaii is getting away from the city.

00:31:03.740 --> 00:31:08.310
Oh, no kidding. It's so easy to relax here. It's like paradise, really.

00:31:08.490 --> 00:31:12.470
It really is. All the left education, all the natural beauty. It's really great.

00:31:12.650 --> 00:31:15.750
Oh, it's beautiful. I can't wait to go out and try some surfing.

00:31:16.050 --> 00:31:19.910
Andy, look! It's our favorite characters from Magnum P.I.

00:31:20.300 --> 00:31:22.000
Yeah, TC and Rip!

00:31:33.870 --> 00:31:34.710
What kind of stuff can you see in there?

00:31:35.240 --> 00:31:42.330
Oh, you know, New York stuff, Wall Street, Twin Towers, two monkeys doing it.

00:31:43.810 --> 00:31:45.590
Two monkeys doing it?

00:31:46.860 --> 00:31:56.930
I'm standing in front of the legendary Sun Studio right here in downtown Memphis, and

00:31:56.930 --> 00:32:00.000
I came here because I wanted to record a song.

00:32:00.960 --> 00:32:08.410
about being a talk show host

00:32:20.780 --> 00:32:27.840
let's try one more time

00:32:53.770 --> 00:33:00.000
made into a CD. Get a shot of that. I'm pretty excited about it. What I'd like you to do is maybe play

00:33:00.000 --> 00:33:11.900
a song on your PA system.

00:33:36.910 --> 00:33:41.030
I'm here with Melissa Atheridge from Science and Janis Joplin songs tonight.

00:33:48.510 --> 00:33:57.880
Need our help, gotta time to help, gotta reach out and lend them a hand.

00:34:00.640 --> 00:34:30.000
We got to each other, sister, uncle, and brother, animals, too, we can help with your needs, people with alien beings, help, help, help, self-testing.

00:34:39.310 --> 00:34:47.370
There's one thing I wanted to talk to you about in that, you know, the part of the song where, you know, you get all worked up that, uh, I want to say, uh, I want to say bye.

00:34:47.790 --> 00:34:49.310
Yeah, yeah, right, right.

00:34:49.550 --> 00:34:52.910
Maybe, maybe Sting should sing that part.

00:34:56.010 --> 00:34:59.230
It just seems like kind of a natural for him.

00:35:00.090 --> 00:35:04.190
Sting really thought of, though, as like a singing guy, like a guy who's a singer.

00:35:05.050 --> 00:35:07.810
He's a bass player.

00:35:07.950 --> 00:35:09.550
I mean, he's Sting.

00:35:09.670 --> 00:35:10.710
Fine, fine.

00:35:11.010 --> 00:35:13.370
Why don't you just, maybe, just, yeah, Sting.

00:35:13.630 --> 00:35:17.290
Let's make it all about, like, people really want to see Sting, you know?

00:35:17.990 --> 00:35:18.430
I'm sorry.

00:35:18.430 --> 00:35:23.750
Let's be, do our best, put our sin.

00:35:38.540 --> 00:35:42.540
the places we've been, the things we've seen.

00:35:42.540 --> 00:35:45.670
You know, Andy, did I mention, by the way,

00:35:45.670 --> 00:35:47.670
I tell you, we got, throughout the show so far,

00:35:47.670 --> 00:35:50.670
we've been getting a lot of congratulatory telegrams.

00:35:50.670 --> 00:35:51.670
That's excellent.

00:35:51.670 --> 00:35:53.670
Just lots of telegrams of congratulations,

00:35:53.670 --> 00:35:55.670
and one in particular is really cool.

00:35:55.670 --> 00:35:56.670
Listen to this.

00:35:56.670 --> 00:35:58.670
Congratulations, Conan and Andy.

00:35:58.670 --> 00:35:59.670
You guys are great.

00:36:00.060 --> 00:36:01.420
Keep up the good work.

00:36:01.730 --> 00:36:04.150
And I thought, that's such a nice telegram.

00:36:04.250 --> 00:36:07.130
I think we should go and thank this guy personally.

00:36:07.290 --> 00:36:07.830
Are you up for it?

00:36:07.950 --> 00:36:08.510
Let's do it.

00:36:08.530 --> 00:36:09.370
Let's do it right now.

00:36:09.470 --> 00:36:10.550
Screw it on over here, Andy.

00:36:10.960 --> 00:36:11.620
Get in there.

00:36:24.100 --> 00:36:24.540
Swedes.

00:36:24.800 --> 00:36:26.930
We'll get out of the studio.

00:36:27.170 --> 00:36:27.730
See you, fellas.

00:36:27.810 --> 00:36:28.880
Be back in just a couple of minutes.

00:36:29.640 --> 00:36:29.880
Yes.

00:36:45.200 --> 00:36:52.500
- There we go, let's go.

00:37:01.120 --> 00:37:01.960
- Good to see ya.

00:37:01.960 --> 00:37:17.520
- How are you?

00:37:17.520 --> 00:37:18.310
- Something really funny to say,

00:37:18.310 --> 00:37:20.150
but you killed the Cucar guy.

00:37:20.150 --> 00:37:22.030
- Yeah, I'm really sorry about that,

00:37:22.030 --> 00:37:23.390
but thanks for the telegram.

00:37:23.390 --> 00:37:24.470
- I'm just kidding.

00:37:24.470 --> 00:37:25.440
- Sorry, Jay.

00:37:25.440 --> 00:37:26.280
We apologize.

00:37:26.280 --> 00:37:27.120
- Bye.

00:37:27.120 --> 00:37:28.480
- Yeah, folks, we'll be right back

00:37:28.480 --> 00:37:29.320
with more after this.

00:37:29.320 --> 00:37:30.000
Sorry.

00:37:30.220 --> 00:38:00.000
And uh, my next guest appeared on our very first...

00:38:00.000 --> 00:38:04.090
first show and he's been a good friend of ours ever since. You know him best as Norm

00:38:04.090 --> 00:38:08.950
on Cheers. Please welcome, ladies and gentlemen, Karl Oldey Olsen.

00:38:08.950 --> 00:38:22.610
My dear friend, my heart sings to be with you on this momentous occasion.

00:38:22.610 --> 00:38:25.410
Thank you, you know what, we wouldn't have done this without you.

00:38:25.410 --> 00:38:30.000
Oh, your hospitality and the felicitations you extend me.

00:38:30.250 --> 00:38:32.010
I'm most appreciated.

00:38:32.650 --> 00:38:37.650
Well, you know, uh, Carl, you've been a big part of the show, and I, uh...

00:38:37.650 --> 00:38:42.570
So I have, but so has violence.

00:38:42.970 --> 00:38:53.740
And the next clip is all about violence, violence, violence, sweet violence.

00:39:00.890 --> 00:39:02.490
Let's, uh, roll the clip, Liz.

00:39:03.050 --> 00:39:03.940
He's creeping me out.

00:39:04.420 --> 00:39:05.950
This is a great birthday.

00:39:14.700 --> 00:39:15.140
Exactly.

00:39:15.760 --> 00:39:16.760
What does he do?

00:39:17.990 --> 00:39:19.260
You want to know what I do?

00:39:20.160 --> 00:39:21.380
This is what I do.

00:39:51.180 --> 00:39:53.000
Great show for you tonight, don't we, Andy?

00:39:53.180 --> 00:39:53.820
We sure do.

00:39:53.900 --> 00:39:56.340
And let's just make it an easy one for my sake, okay?

00:39:56.640 --> 00:39:58.620
Because, you know, I'm two days away from retirement.

00:39:59.000 --> 00:39:59.780
Oh, that's right.

00:40:00.030 --> 00:40:05.830
special plans? I'm just going to sail to Barbados and take it easy. Wow, how I envy you.

00:40:43.080 --> 00:40:44.020
Thank you.

00:41:01.530 --> 00:41:04.450
Our first guest tonight is my favorite Roker weatherman.

00:41:04.950 --> 00:41:07.590
Please welcome a friend to us all, Al Roker.

00:41:08.070 --> 00:41:10.820
I love you, homie.

00:41:11.270 --> 00:41:12.210
We couldn't do it without you.

00:41:12.230 --> 00:41:13.170
We'll be right back, folks.

00:41:13.230 --> 00:41:13.670
Stick around.

00:41:35.690 --> 00:41:40.390
third anniversary show. I do want to take a second here and thank all the great guests

00:41:40.390 --> 00:41:47.720
that helped us out tonight. Thank you all very much for doing it. I also want to thank

00:41:47.720 --> 00:41:54.410
our incredibly amazing staff and crew that make this show, you know, as good as it is

00:41:54.410 --> 00:41:58.770
every night. I want to thank what I think is the best band in TV, the Max Weinberg Seven,

00:42:02.720 --> 00:42:09.080
I want to thank both Dave and Jay for always being so gracious to this show and helping us out.

00:42:09.440 --> 00:42:13.280
And the unfailingly hysterical Andy Richter for always being so friendly.

00:42:16.110 --> 00:42:18.440
We've been hurt now.

00:42:18.920 --> 00:42:20.500
Anyway, thanks to everybody.

00:42:20.900 --> 00:42:22.160
We'll see you Monday. Bye-bye.

00:42:35.690 --> 00:42:36.310
Saddam.
